     "A study finds that students who own a laptop get better grades than students who do not. The laptops are not the reason: richer families are the ones who buy their children laptops, and the same families also pay for tutors and quiet rooms to study in.",
     "A city's ice cream shop opens a second branch near the public pool. Sales are steady, the lifeguards stop by for cones after work, and the owner hires two students for the season.",
     "During a heat wave, every ice cream shop and home in the city runs its freezers and air conditioners at full power at once. The power grid overloads, one station trips, its load shifts to the next, which trips too, and within an hour the whole city is dark.",
     "A study finds that students who own a laptop get better grades than students who do not. The laptops are the reason: poorer families buy their children laptops as often as richer ones, and only students with one can do the online homework the school sets.",
